THE FOUNDING CHARTER OF MATHEMATICAL FUTUROLOGICAL MEDICINE

A Formal Axiomatic Framework for Mathematical Futurology, Personalized Medicine, Longevity, and Evidence-Based Therapeutics

Founding Principle

Mathematical Futurological Medicine (MFM) is the discipline of applying mathematics, formal logic, statistics, computation, biological science, chemistry, and predictive modeling to the future optimization of human health.

Its fundamental objective is:

[
\boxed{
\max_{\mathcal{I}}
E[\text{Human Healthspan}+\text{Quality of Life}]
}
]

subject to:

[
\boxed{
\text{Safety} \geq \text{acceptable threshold}
}
]

and

[
\boxed{
\text{Scientific claims} \Rightarrow \text{evidence}
}
]

MFM therefore rejects both uncritical faith in medication and uncritical rejection of medication.

Its fundamental question is not:

“Are medicines good or bad?”

but:

[
\boxed{
\text{Which intervention maximizes expected benefit for this particular person under these particular conditions?}
}
]

