ARTICLE VI — THE MEDICATION PRINCIPLE

MFM does not establish:

[
Medication=Bad.
]

Nor does it establish:

[
Medication=Good.
]

Instead:

[
\boxed{
Net\ Expected\ Value

Expected\ Benefit

Expected\ Harm
}
]

A medication should therefore be evaluated according to:

[
V(D,i,C)

B(D,i,C)

R(D,i,C)

C(D,i,C)
]

where:

* (B) = expected benefit
* (R) = expected medical risk
* (C) = burden/cost.

