ARTICLE VIII — THE N-OF-1 PRINCIPLE

Every sufficiently measured individual represents a longitudinal biological dataset.

For person (i):

[
X_i(t)\rightarrow Y_i(t).
]

The system seeks to estimate:

[
ATE_i(D)

E[Y_i|D]-E[Y_i|Control].
]

This represents an individualized treatment effect rather than merely an average population effect.

Population evidence remains essential; individual observations supplement rather than automatically replace controlled evidence.

