ARTICLE X — CHEMICAL REACTION AS SYMBOLIC LOGIC

For a reaction:

[
A+B\rightarrow C+D
]

define:

Premise 1

[
A\land B\land K
]

where (K) represents the necessary reaction conditions.

Premise 2

[
Conservation(A,B,C,D)
]

Premise 3

[
Evidence(A,B,K\Rightarrow C,D)
]

Conclusion

[
\therefore
A+B
\xrightarrow{K}
C+D.
]

This is the formal structure of the MFM chemical proposition.

