ARTICLE XI — ARISTOTELIAN SYLLOGISTIC MANUFACTURING LOGIC

Every assumption in a pharmaceutical manufacturing model shall be explicitly labeled.

The canonical form is:

Major Premise — A

A universally asserted proposition.

Minor Premise — B

A proposition establishing that the particular case belongs to the universal class.

Conclusion — C

The logically derived consequence.

Formally:

[
A\rightarrow C
]

[
B\subseteq A
]

therefore:

[
\boxed{B\rightarrow C}
]

