ARTICLE XIV — THE EVIDENCE AXIOM

No mathematical elegance can substitute for empirical evidence.

A proposition (P) receives evidentiary weight:

[
W(P)=f(
Replication,
SampleSize,
StudyDesign,
MeasurementQuality,
Bias,
Consistency
).
]

A beautiful equation with no empirical support remains a hypothesis.

[
\boxed{
Mathematical\ sophistication\neq Scientific\ validation
}
]

